<?xml version="1.0"?>
<?xml-model href="./FlowConfig.rng"?>
<!-- Hand-written, unlike the federal modules beside it, which are transpiler output. Named
     {category}-{subcategory}.xml like them, under the 'your-taxes' category, so the port's FlowSpec
     conventions hold: routes start /your-taxes/virginia/. Every screen is gated on /vaIsResident.
     The order is the design: what is already known, grouped by where it came from; then the four
     things only the filer can answer; then the return. Figures come from facts/virginia.xml and
     facts/virginiaLocalities.xml; see docs/adr/001-virginia-state-return.md. -->
<FlowConfig>
  <page title="Your Virginia return" route="/your-taxes/virginia/virginia-intro">
    <section>
      <div class="df-screen" condition="/vaIsResident" operator="isTrue">
        <h2>Your Virginia return</h2>
        <p><strong>Demonstration only.</strong> This is a class project showing how a state return could be computed from the federal return on the IRS's published code. It is not an IRS or Virginia Tax service and files nothing.</p>
        <p><fg-show path="/primaryFiler/firstName"/>, because you lived in Virginia for all of <fg-show path="/taxYear"/>, most of your Virginia return is already done. Form 760 starts from your federal return, your employer already sent Virginia your W-2, and Virginia Tax already holds what you have paid. The next screen shows what is known. After that, four questions no one reports for you, and then your return.</p>
        <p>What this prototype covers: the standard deduction, exemptions, the age deduction, the filing threshold, the rate schedule, withholding, two Schedule ADJ items (lottery prizes and Commonwealth Savers contributions), the locality code and the consumer's use tax (Va. Code §§ 58.1-320, 58.1-321, 58.1-322.02, 58.1-322.03). What it leaves out: itemized deductions, the other additions and subtractions, every credit, part-year and nonresident returns, and a spouse's share of anything.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </page>
  <page title="What is already known" route="/your-taxes/virginia/virginia-known">
    <section>
      <div class="df-screen" condition="/vaIsResident" operator="isTrue">
        <h2>What is already known</h2>
        <p>Grouped by where it came from. These are the facts your Virginia return is computed from. To correct one, go back to the screen where you entered it; the correction reaches both returns.</p>
        <table class="usa-table usa-table--borderless">
          <caption>From your federal return</caption>
          <tr><th scope="row">Name</th><td><fg-show path="/primaryFiler/firstName"/> <fg-show path="/primaryFiler/lastName"/></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Filing status</th><td><fg-show path="/filingStatus"/></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Date of birth</th><td><fg-show path="/primaryFiler/dateOfBirth"/></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Federal adjusted gross income (Form 1040 line 11)</th><td><fg-show path="/agi"/></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Taxable Social Security (line 6b)</th><td><fg-show path="/taxableSocialSecurityBenefits"/></td></tr>
        </table>
        <table class="usa-table usa-table--borderless">
          <caption>From the W-2s your employer filed with the IRS and with Virginia</caption>
          <tr><th scope="row">Box 1, wages, all W-2s</th><td><fg-show path="/wages"/></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Box 17, Virginia tax withheld, all W-2s (Line 19a)</th><td><fg-show path="/vaWithholding"/></td></tr>
        </table>
        <table class="usa-table usa-table--borderless">
          <caption>From Virginia Tax's own records</caption>
          <tr><th scope="row">Estimated payments made for <fg-show path="/taxYear"/> (Line 20)</th><td><fg-show path="/vaEstimatedPayments"/></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Last year's overpayment applied (Line 21)</th><td><fg-show path="/vaPriorYearOverpaymentApplied"/></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Extension payments (Line 22)</th><td><fg-show path="/vaExtensionPayments"/></td></tr>
        </table>
        <p>In a state-run service the last three come from Virginia Tax's books. This prototype has no connection to them, so they are shown as $0.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </page>
  <page title="Is everything right?" route="/your-taxes/virginia/virginia-check">
    <section>
      <div class="df-screen" condition="/vaIsResident" operator="isTrue">
        <h2>Is everything on the last screen right?</h2>
        <p>If something is wrong, say so here and you will be taken to correct it. Your Virginia return and your federal return share the same facts, so a correction made here reaches both, and you will not be asked about it again.</p>
        <fg-set path="/vaEverythingRight">
          <question>Is everything right?</question>
          <input type="boolean">
            <option value="true">Yes, everything is right</option>
            <option value="false">No, something needs correcting</option>
          </input>
        </fg-set>
      </div>
    </section>
  </page>
  <page title="What needs correcting?" route="/your-taxes/virginia/virginia-correct-what">
    <section>
      <div class="df-screen" condition="/vaWantsToCorrect" operator="isTrue">
        <h2>What needs correcting?</h2>
        <p>Pick one. You can come back for another. Calculated amounts such as your adjusted gross income cannot be edited; they change when what they are calculated from changes.</p>
        <fg-set path="/vaCorrectionTarget">
          <question>What needs correcting?</question>
          <input type="enum" options-path="/vaCorrectionTargetOptions">
            <option value="dateOfBirth">My date of birth</option>
            <option value="w2">A W-2 from my employer</option>
          </input>
        </fg-set>
      </div>
    </section>
  </page>
  <page title="Correct your date of birth" route="/your-taxes/virginia/virginia-correct-dob">
    <section>
      <div class="df-screen" condition="/vaCorrectionTargetIsDateOfBirth" operator="isTrue">
        <h2>Correct your date of birth</h2>
        <p>We have <fg-show path="/primaryFiler/dateOfBirth"/>, from your federal return. <strong>This also updates your federal return.</strong> Virginia uses it for the age deduction and the 65-or-older exemption.</p>
        <fg-set path="/primaryFiler/dateOfBirth">
          <question>Correct date of birth</question>
          <input type="date"/>
        </fg-set>
      </div>
    </section>
  </page>
  <page title="Correct a W-2" route="/your-taxes/virginia/virginia-correct-w2">
    <section>
      <div class="df-screen" condition="/vaCorrectionTargetIsW2" operator="isTrue">
        <h2>Correct your W-2</h2>
        <p><strong>Check the paper W-2 first.</strong> Your employer reported these boxes to the IRS and to Virginia. If the W-2 itself is wrong, ask your employer for a corrected one (a W-2c). If you change a box here without one, Virginia will see a difference from what your employer sent and may write to you about it.</p>
        <p>Boxes 1 and 2 also update your federal return. Boxes 16 and 17 are the ones Virginia uses: your Virginia wages and the tax already withheld.</p>
        <fg-collection path="/formW2s" item-name="W-2" determiner="another">
          <div class="df-screen">
            <h2>W-2 from <fg-show path="/formW2s/*/employerName"/></h2>
            <fg-set path="/formW2s/*/employerName">
              <question>Employer name</question>
              <input type="text"/>
            </fg-set>
            <fg-set path="/formW2s/*/writableWages" optional="true">
              <question><strong>Box 1</strong> - Wages, tips, other compensation</question>
              <input type="dollar"/>
            </fg-set>
            <fg-set path="/formW2s/*/writableFederalWithholding" optional="true">
              <question><strong>Box 2</strong> - Federal income tax withheld</question>
              <input type="dollar"/>
            </fg-set>
            <fg-set path="/formW2s/*/writableStateWages" optional="true">
              <question><strong>Box 16</strong> - State wages, tips, etc.</question>
              <input type="dollar"/>
            </fg-set>
            <fg-set path="/formW2s/*/writableStateWithholding" optional="true">
              <question><strong>Box 17</strong> - State income tax withheld</question>
              <input type="dollar"/>
            </fg-set>
          </div>
        </fg-collection>
      </div>
    </section>
  </page>
  <page title="Your correction" route="/your-taxes/virginia/virginia-corrections">
    <section>
      <div class="df-screen" condition="/vaWantsToCorrect" operator="isTrue">
        <h2>Your correction is saved. Here is what it changed.</h2>
        <div class="va-corrections-diff"><p>Comparing your return before and after the correction.</p></div>
        <p><strong>What stays the same.</strong> Everything else you saw is unchanged, and nothing you have already answered will be asked again. Your federal return carries the same correction. To correct something else, go back to "Is everything right?" and choose again.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </page>
